WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.280
Now that we've all binged Stranger Things
3, let's talk about the season's ending.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.960
Toast some Eggos, turn on the boombox, and
watch out for the Mind Flayer.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.991
From shocking deaths to shifts in the status
quo to what we can expect from season 4, this

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.720
is the ending of Stranger Things 3, explained.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.940
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.960
After a lengthy battle, Stranger Things 3
ends with an emotional departure, as the Byers

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.800
family sells their little house in Hawkins
for a new life somewhere else.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.840
Will has to say goodbye to his friends, Jonathan
has to say goodbye to Nancy, and El has to

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.800
say goodbye to Mike and the life she'd been
building with Hopper.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.899
We don't know exactly where the family will
settle, but it's a tearful upheaval that changes

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.880
the landscape of the show forever.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.920
This whole story began with four friends Mike,
Will, Dustin, and Lucas as they were swept

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.160
up in an otherworldly adventure after a night
of playing Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.380
Now, at the end of Stranger Things 3, the
state of "The Party" has changed in a major

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.180
way.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.300
Will the gang reunite in season 4?

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.880
What could bring Joyce, Jonathan, Will, and
Eleven back to Hawkins?

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.580
Perhaps another crisis taking place over a
holiday celebration?

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.300
"And then I was thinking maybe you could come
out here for Christmas.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.400
You could come before or after Christmas,
or whatever Mrs. Byers wants."

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.980
The "Three Months Later" epilogue for the
last episode of Stranger Things 3 begins with

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.340
a clip from a news report that suggests the
dark and mysterious goings-on of Hawkins are

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.820
becoming publicly known in some way.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.960
In the past, the government's been able to
keep a relatively tight lid on things but

00:01:27.969 --> 00:01:28.969
not anymore.

00:01:28.969 --> 00:01:32.950
Now, with the town's mayor in handcuffs and
reports of everything from chemical leaks

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.440
to the tragedy at Starcourt making the rounds,
Hawkins is gaining a reputation on a national

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.220
level.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.420
Shortly before Stranger Things 3's final battle
at Starcourt, Eleven poured every drop of

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:47.900
telekinetic energy she had into ripping the
last shred of the Mind Flayer out of her.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.500
In the wake of that effort, she was unable
to even crush an empty soda can with her mind.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.800
At the time she seemed to think she just need
to recharge, as she always has.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.680
But then the season's epilogue revealed that
she still didn't have her powers back after

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.780
three months.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.180
Does this mean her powers are gone forever?

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.260
It's possible, but unlikely.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.720
The series gets far too much mileage out of
El's superpowers, so while we may end up waiting

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:15.450
a long while for Eleven to find her mojo again,
her powerless era may let her take some time

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.140
to learn a little more about being a regular
teenager.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.560
The season's post-credits sequence reveals
that the Soviets have managed to capture a

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.300
Demogorgon, and they're keeping it alive in
a cell by feeding it a steady diet of prisoners.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.960
What exactly they plan to do with it is anyone's
guess, but it can't be good.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.000
This is all made even creepier by the fact
that we still don't know exactly what the

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:41.280
Russians hoped to do with the knowledge gained
by opening the gate, or how they managed to

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.760
figure out so much about how to get into it
in the first place.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.540
Are there more Russian spies working on this
exact problem embedded in Hawkins right now?

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.820
Is their tech strong enough to open a new
gate now that they've had time to work on

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:53.820
it?

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.580
Can that corrosive green liquid be used to
power anything else?

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.920
Can the Demogorgon become a trained killer?

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.640
There are so many questions here, and none
of them have happy answers.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.580
Chief Jim Hopper lived through a lot on Stranger
Things, but he couldn't really survive the

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.080
explosion of the Key at the end of the season.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.900
He knew it was necessary for Joyce to blow
it up as quickly as possible.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.380
It was a noble sacrifice, and a fitting end
for a great character.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.660
Or was it?

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:23.480
The post-credits scene makes it clear that
the Soviets have someone in their cells they

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.280
refer to as "the American."

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.340
Could that unseen American be Hopper?

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.500
Consider this: the show goes to great pains
to show us how destructive the Key explosion

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.400
is.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.180
It shows us several Russian scientists who
are flat-out vaporized by its power but it

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.540
never shows the same thing happening to Hopper.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.099
This show has shown us the corpses of everyone
from Bob to Barb to Billy over the course

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.600
of three seasons to make sure we knew those
characters were dead, but we never see Hopper's

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.480
body.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.400
Is that because there isn't one?

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.280
If it's really true, he's going to have a
honey of a story to tell when he gets back

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.440
to the States.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.980
Then again, there's another potential candidate
for the Soviets' American prisoner: Doctor

00:04:06.989 --> 00:04:12.150
Brenner, Eleven's "Papa," who we were told
in season 2 isn't as dead and buried as we

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.520
previously thought:

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:14.800
"Brenner!

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.920
I can take you to him."

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.300
"Papa is gone."

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.320
"No, he is alive."

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.240
Stranger Things 3 doesn't end in a self-contained
way.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.880
Its many dangling plot threads, from the future
of the Byers family to what exactly might

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.730
be going on in Russia, all suggest a sense
of a continuing story, and that is indeed

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.600
the plan.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.840
According to an Entertainment Weekly interview
with Stranger Things executive producer Shawn

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:44.530
Levy, the current plan for the series is for
creators Matt and Ross Duffer to tell a story

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.780
that lasts at least four seasons, if not five.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.000
So we should definitely expect more from the
Hawkins gang.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.740
The real question now isn't if, but when.

